<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Seychelles</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Seychelles is an archipelago in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a>, which was a British colony from the early nineteenth century. The British used it as a place of exile for deposed rulers. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashanti-empire">Ashanti Empire</a> note that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asantehene">Asantehene</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prempeh-i">Prempeh I</a> was exiled to the Seychelles after the British occupation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kumasi">Kumasi</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/seychelles.jpg" alt="Seychelles" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vxb83 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Seychelles.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 1896, in the Fourth Anglo-Ashanti War, a British expedition occupied Kumasi without a fight and deposed Asantehene Prempeh I, who was exiled first to Sierra Leone and from 1900 to the <b>Seychelles</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/ashanti-empire">Ashanti Empire · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>Kabalega was captured in 1899 together with Mwanga, the deposed king of Buganda, a long-time rival who had become his ally; the British exiled both men to the <b>Seychelles</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-bunyoro">Kingdom of Bunyoro · At a glance</a></li><li><blockquote>The French-settled <b>Seychelles</b> surrendered to British warships several times during the Napoleonic Wars, while the French commandant Quéau de Quinssy stayed on to run the islands.</blockquote><a href="/state/british-seychelles">British Seychelles</a></li></ul></section>
